course: dictionary
lesson: 7437
title: Pollution
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pollution is a noun you cannot count, so you say «some pollution», not «three pollutions». When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues.
explain: «Light pollution, light from cities, hides the Milky Way from most people who live in towns.» The words «light from cities» are the clue. Light is not the problem on its own, but too much unwanted light from towns spoils the view of the stars, so pollution means something harmful that spoils things.
explain: «The factories also filled the air with smoke and dirtied rivers, the start of the pollution problems we still deal with today.» Smoke, dirty rivers and problems are the clues. Pollution means dirt and harmful waste in the air or water.
explain: A good check is to swap a simpler meaning into the sentence. Try «dirt»: «the start of the dirt problems we still deal with today» still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
fact: Pollution is harmful material put into air, water or soil.
fact: «Pollution» can mean dirt, poison or waste that harms living things, or the act of making things dirty and harmful.
fact: Noise pollution and light pollution are unwanted noise or light, such as «light from cities» that hides the stars at night.
fact: Frogs breathe partly through their thin, moist skin, so they are harmed quickly by pollution.
fact: Lessons on pollution explain how to reduce it: recycle, walk, and use less plastic.
exercise: «Light pollution, light from cities, hides the Milky Way from most people who live in towns.» What does light pollution hide from most town people? | The bus timetable | Their shadows | Their dinner | *The Milky Way
exercise: Which of these is an example of pollution? | A sunny picnic in the park | A quiet walk in the woods | *Smoke from factories filling the air | Recycling old paper
exercise: «Frogs are harmed quickly by pollution.» Why are frogs harmed quickly? | Because their skin is thick and dry | *Because they breathe partly through thin, moist skin | Because they live in deserts | Because they cannot swim
test: «Noise pollution» is a phrase. In it, what does pollution mean? | Dirty smoke | *Unwanted noise | A type of fish | Clean water
test: Which of these helps to reduce pollution? | Leaving lights on all night | Burning rubbish in the garden | Dropping litter in rivers | *Using less plastic
exam: Which sentence uses pollution to mean dirt in air or water? | *Smoke from the factory dirtied the river | The stars were bright tonight | We went to the park on Sunday | The sky was clear and blue
